id: date/utc/2769
area: date
op: Date.parse, the Date Time String Format
in: str:"0001"
out: value: f64:0xC2CC4189166C0000
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: A date-only form of the Date Time String Format for a year from 0001 to 9999 is read as local time, where it is UTC; the difference shows in a zone whose offset at that date is not zero, such as America/New_York, and not under UTC. Answered by Broiler.JS docs/roadmap/SharedLibraries.md, SJL-6.5 (the Date area's record; the correspondence's row P1).
